# Two peers. drone-1 reboots twice from its boot image, each time resuming at boot epoch + 1: the first reboot is what
# an honest host does; the second is a host whose epoch write never reached storage, so it hands the same epoch out
# again and the drone's first replies after it carry nonces it already used. gcs sees them as duplicates of wires it
# accepted before, the calls expire, and traffic recovers once the counter passes where the first life ended. That
# silent loss, and the keystream reuse beneath it, is why the epoch is written before a peer may speak.
seed 41
peers 2
profile dtn
20000  stale_reboot 1
50000  stale_reboot 1
